    "updated_at": "2025-10-30T09:03:17Z",
    "body": "So for context, what I did on Gecko is: at the same time we try to focus `b` (after we've blurred `a`), if we realize we can't (because we have moved focus somewhere else), fix up the `:focus-within` state and remove it from `parent` if needed, see the patches in the bug linked in the OP.",
